# Get started

To get started with Giolt, first install the Giolt SDK:

```
$ gleam add --dev giolt_sdk
```

The Giolt SDK provides command-line tools for building your app with Giolt.
To build your app, run:

```
$ gleam run -m giolt build
```

With an `entry_module` configured, this creates a `./dist` folder containing the entrypoint to your app.

[Read the full Giolt SDK reference](/sdk)

## SDK configuration

The Giolt SDK is configured from `gleam.toml`:

```toml
# gleam.toml
[tools.giolt]
outdir = "./dist"
static_dir = "./public"
entry_module = "app"
bundle_aliases = [
    "@gleam=./build/dev/javascript"
]
```

